{"parentUuid":"e0496887-5c4a-49c9-a21e-f7347824d813","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XdX6UNbJTFNwPyWaL7Dvrz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough evidence to answer. Short version: **no, it won't auto-pick up**, but a shared config is straightforward.\n\n## What Entire writes for Gemini\n\n`cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go:60` writes to **`<repo>/.gemini/settings.json`** with this nested shape:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"hooksConfig\": { \"enabled\": true },\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"SessionStart\": [{ \"hooks\": [{ \"name\": \"entire-session-start\", \"type\": \"command\", \"command\": \"entire hooks gemini session-start\" }] }],\n    \"BeforeTool\":   [{ \"matcher\": \"*\", \"hooks\": [{ \"name\": \"entire-before-tool\", \"type\": \"command\", \"command\": \"entire hooks gemini before-tool\" }] }],\n    ...11 events total\n  }\n}\n```\n\nEvent names are PascalCase: `SessionStart`, `SessionEnd`, `BeforeAgent`/`AfterAgent`, `BeforeModel`/`AfterModel`, `BeforeToolSelection`, `BeforeTool`/`AfterTool`, `PreCompress`, `Notification` (`geminicli/hooks.go:22-34`).\n\n## What Antigravity expects (per your doc quote)\n\n- **File:** `hooks.json` (standalone, not nested under `settings.json`)\n- **Path:** `.agents/hooks.json` (workspace) or `~/.gemini/config/hooks.json` (user)\n\nThe Antigravity site is an Angular SPA so I couldn't pull the full schema, but the bundled strings confirm \"JSON Hooks\" and at least a `sessionstart` event, and the Google Developers blog explicitly says Hooks are \"carried over\" but with \"not 1:1 feature parity right out of the gate.\"\n\n## So: will it work automatically?\n\n**No.** Two hard mismatches:\n\n1. **Different file & location** — Antigravity reads `.agents/hooks.json` or `~/.gemini/config/hooks.json`; Entire writes `.gemini/settings.json`.\n2. **Different shape** — Entire's hooks live *nested* under `\"hooks\": {...}` inside `settings.json`. A standalone `hooks.json` is presumably the hook block hoisted to top level (and possibly with renamed/different event names — I couldn't confirm).\n\nA symlink won't bridge it because of #2.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- Entire's installer is already structured to make this easy to extend: `InstallHooks` parses → mutates → re-serializes, and the per-event commands are computed via `cmdPrefix + \"<event>\"`. A second writer that targets a different path + flatter schema can reuse most of that code.\n- The marker for \"is this our hook?\" is `entireHookPrefixes` (`hooks.go:40`) — sharing that lets uninstall/idempotency work across both locations without drift.\n- Per-event command name reuse means we can keep one set of `entire hooks gemini <event>` subcommands and just point Antigravity at them, provided Antigravity's stdin payload shape matches Gemini's (this we'd need to verify before shipping).\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n## Options for sharing"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18577,"cache_read_input_tokens":105985,"output_tokens":3057,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18577,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3057,"cache_read_input_tokens":105985,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18577,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18577},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CbCWFuCKii5aXSnmAwGPV","type":"assistant","uuid":"c75e7592-9054-4701-a457-74a7f33ca81d","timestamp":"2026-05-19T19:48:25.370Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli","sessionId":"27c10fbd-3055-4d96-8e88-8a95ee2d9e1e","version":"2.1.144","gitBranch":"main"}
