erPromptSubmit, Stop, StopFailure), and on every tool call inside the agentic loop (PreToolUse, PostToolUse).\n\n### Hook Input via stdin\n\nClaude Code sends event context as JSON on stdin, passing JSON context about the event to your hook handler, with input arriving on stdin for command hooks.\n\n### Hook Event Names and Schema\n\nThe search results reference multiple hook events including:\n- **SessionStart** / **SessionEnd** - Session lifecycle\n- **PreToolUse** / **PostToolUse** - Tool execution events  \n- **UserPromptSubmit** - User input events\n- **Stop** / **StopFailure** - Stop conditions\n- **PermissionRequest** - Permission control\n\n### Payload Structure\n\nWhen a PreToolUse event fires, Claude Code sends tool input as JSON on stdin including tool_name, tool_input, and other context. For PreToolUse, the stdin payload includes session_id, cwd, hook_event_name, tool_name, tool_input with the command, and tool_use_id.\n\n### Hook Configuration Files\n\nInstalled plugins can bundle lifecycle config through a default hooks/hooks.json file, and if a single layer contains both hooks.json and inline [hooks], the system merges them.\n\nThe search results primarily focus on Claude Code hooks rather than \"antigravity\" specifically, though there are references to Antigravity as a Google product for code assistance.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"78e7ca41-a567-4efd-a8b3-22ae068aaf7b","timestamp":"2026-05-19T19:52:44.527Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"\"antigravity\" CLI \"hooks.json\" schema event names tool_use stdin payload","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01BHyGV6JvYK3v4wMztEkqg1","content":[{"title":"fix(ai): Claude via Antigravity 400s — tool schemas use unsupported JSON Schema features · Issue #2255 · badlogic/pi-mono","url":"https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/issues/2255"},{"title":"Hooks reference - Claude Code Docs","url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks"},{"