igravity/lifecycle.go`\n792\t- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/lifecycle_test.go`\n793\t\n794\tThe contract here (per `agent.go:88-104`) is `HookNames() []string` + `ParseHookEvent(ctx, hookName, stdin) (*Event, error)`. We do NOT define standalone `HandleX` functions — the framework drives the subcommand dispatch and calls `ParseHookEvent`. We return a normalized `agent.Event` (or `nil` for hooks with no lifecycle significance).\n795\t\n796\t**Event mapping (Antigravity → Entire):**\n797\t\n798\t| Antigravity hook | Returned `Event.Type` |\n799\t|---|---|\n800\t| `pre-invocation` | `agent.TurnStart` (always — the framework's TurnStart handler calls `strategy.InitializeSession` at `cli/lifecycle.go:406`, which is idempotent; first arrival creates state, subsequent arrivals reuse it) |\n801\t| `post-invocation` | `agent.TurnEnd` |\n802\t| `stop` (fullyIdle=true) | `agent.SessionEnd` |\n803\t| `stop` (fullyIdle=false) | `nil` (background tasks still running) |\n804\t| `pre-tool-use` | `agent.ToolUse` with extracted `ModifiedFiles`/`NewFiles` for `write_to_file`/`replace_file_content`/`multi_replace_file_content`; `nil` for non-mutating tools |\n805\t| `post-tool-use` | `nil` (PreToolUse already captured file impact) |\n806\t\n807\t**Decision: no explicit SessionStart event in v1.** Antigravity has no SessionStart hook surface. The natural map would be \"first PreInvocation → SessionStart, then later TurnStart on the next one\" — but the *first turn's* tool events arrive **between** PreInvocation #1 and PreInvocation #2, before session state would exist. Rather than fire two events from one hook (which `ParseHookEvent`'s `(*Event, error)` contract does not allow), v1 always returns `TurnStart` from PreInvocation. The cost: the SessionStart-only side effects (banner from `handleLifecycleSessionStart` at `cli/lifecycle.go:98-205`) never fire for Antigravity. Document this gap in the Deferred table; a follow-up can fire SessionStart inline before returning TurnStart on first-ever invocation once we confirm the framework tolerates that ordering.\n808\t\n809\tHook constants:\n810\t\n811\t```go\n812\tconst (\n813\t    HookNamePreToolUse     = \"pre-tool-use\"\n814\t    HookNamePostToolUse    = \"post-tool-use\"\n815\t    HookNamePreInvocation  = \"pre-invocation\"\n816\t    HookNamePostInvocation = \"post-invocation\"\n817\t    HookNameStop           = \"stop\"\n818\t)\n819\t```\n820\t\n821\t- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing tests**\n822\t\n823\t```go\n824\t// lifecycle_test.go\n825\tpackage antigravity\n826\t\n827\timport (\n828\t    \"bytes\"\n829\t    \"context\"\n830\t    \"os\"\n831\t    \"path/filepath\"\n832\t    \"strings\"\n833\t    \"testing\"\n834\t\n835\t    \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n836\t    \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/testutil\"\n837\t)\n838\t\n839\tfunc TestHookNames(t *testing.T) {\n840\t    t.Parallel()\n841\t    a := &AntigravityAgent{}\n842\t    names := a.HookNames()\n843\t    want := []string{\"pre-tool-use\", \"post-tool-use\", \"pre-invocation\", \"post-invocation\", \"stop\"}\n844\t    if len(names) != len(want) { t.Fatalf(\"got %d, want %d\", len(names), len(want)) }\n845\t    // ... iterate to compare\n846\t}\n847\t\n848\tfunc TestParseHookEvent_PreInvocationEmitsTurnStart(t *testing.T) {\n849\t    t.Parallel()\n850\t    data, _ := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"testdata\", \"hook_stdin_preinvocation.json\"))\n851\t    a := &AntigravityAgent{}\n852\t    ev, err := a.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNamePreInvocation, bytes.NewReader(data))\n853\t    if err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n854\t    if ev == nil || ev.Type != agent.TurnStart {\n855\t        t.Errorf(\"got %v, want TurnStart\", ev)\n856\t    }\n857\t    if ev.SessionID != \"ec33ebf9-0cba-4100-8142-c61503f6c587\" {\n858\t        t.Errorf(\"SessionID = %q\", ev.SessionID)\n859\t    }\n860\t    if !strings.HasSuffix(ev.SessionRef, \"transcript.jsonl\") {\n861\t        t.Errorf(\"SessionRef = %q (want transcrip