{"parentUuid":"43e2443a-61fc-42eb-8fb0-85e082aa1810","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01TgauPu9QwNWwP8ZTYWjYqh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- Smoke testing your own integration is the highest-fidelity verification — automated tests assert that *the code does what the code does*, but only manual driving reveals UX gaps and integration surprises (e.g., banner missing, confusing output, paths that break in real environments).\n- The `entire` CLI is organized around noun groups (`session`, `checkpoint`, `agent`, `auth`, `doctor`) per CLAUDE.md. Each group has verbs that exercise different layers — so a thorough smoke pass touches one verb per group.\n- I already built a binary for the previous smoke tests at `/tmp/entire-smoke` — you can use that or rebuild with `go build -o ~/bin/entire ./cmd/entire` if you want it on PATH.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nStepping back from the finish flow. Here's a hands-on smoke test playbook covering hooks + every command group with the antigravity integration active.\n\n## Setup\n\n```fish\n# Use the binary I already built (or rebuild fresh)\nset -x ENTIRE /tmp/entire-smoke\n# Or for fresh: set -x ENTIRE (mktemp); go build -o $ENTIRE ./cmd/entire\n\n# Fresh throwaway repo\nrm -rf /tmp/agy-smoke\nmkdir /tmp/agy-smoke && cd /tmp/agy-smoke\ngit init -q\ngit config user.email test@example.com\ngit config user.name \"Smoke Test\"\ngit config commit.gpgsign false\necho \"initial\" > README.md\ngit add . && git commit -m \"init\" -q\n```\n\n## Phase 1: Agent registration + install\n\n```fish\n# Listed in picker?\n$ENTIRE agent list\n\n# Install hooks (preview-tagged)\n$ENTIRE agent add antigravity\n\n# Hooks file looks right?\ncat .agents/hooks.json | jq .\n\n# Sanity: NO .gemini/settings.json (we're not Gemini)\ntest -f .gemini/settings.json; and echo \"WRONG\"; or echo \"OK\"\n```\n\n**Expect:** 5 hooks installed, `entire` key in `.agents/hooks.json` with the `sh -c 'if ! command -v entire ...'` wrapper.\n\n## Phase 2: Drive a fake session (no agy needed)\n\nThis simulates Antigravity calling our hooks. The `entire` CLI handles them as if a real agent fired them.\n\n```fish\nset CONV smoke-$(date +%s)\n\n# pre-invocation → TurnStart (creates session state)\necho '{\"conversationId\":\"'$CONV'\",\"workspacePaths\":[\"'$PWD'\"],\"transcriptPath\":\"'$PWD'/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/'$CONV'/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl\",\"artifactDirectoryPath\":\"'$PWD'/.gemini/artifacts\",\"invocationNum\":1,\"initialNumSteps\":0}' | $ENTIRE hooks antigravity pre-invocation\n\n# Pre-stage transcript file (the framework reads it on TurnEnd/SessionEnd)\nmkdir -p .gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/$CONV/.system_generated/logs\necho '{\"step_index\":0,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"content\":\"create foo.txt\"}' > .gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/$CONV/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl\n\n# pre-tool-use write_to_file → records files_touched\necho '{\"conversationId\":\"'$CONV'\",\"workspacePaths\":[\"'$PWD'\"],\"transcriptPath\":\"'$PWD'/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/'$CONV'/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl\",\"artifactDirectoryPath\":\"'$PWD'/.gemini/artifacts\",\"toolCall\":{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"TargetFile\":\"foo.txt\",\"Overwrite\":false}},\"stepIdx\":1}' | $ENTIRE hooks antigravity pre-tool-use\n\n# Actually create the file (simulating what agy would do between hook events)\necho \"hello from foo\" > foo.txt\n\n# post-tool-use (no-op)\necho '{\"conversationId\":\"'$CONV'\",\"workspacePaths\":[\"'$PWD'\"],\"transcriptPath\":\"'$PWD'/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/'$CONV'/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl\",\"artifactDirectoryPath\":\"'$PWD'/.gemini/artifacts\",\"stepIdx\":1}' | $ENTIRE hooks antigravity post-tool-use\n\n# post-invocation → TurnEnd\necho '{\"conversationId\":\"'$CONV'\",\"workspacePaths\":[\"'$PWD'\"],\"transcriptPath\":\"'$PWD'/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/'$CONV'/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl\",\"artifactDirectoryPath\":\"'$PWD'/.gemini/artifacts\",\"invocationNum\":1,\"initialNumSteps\":2}' | $ENTIRE hooks antigravity post-invocation\n\n# stop with fullyIdle=true → SessionEnd\necho '{\"conversationId\":\"'$CONV'\",\"workspacePaths\":[\"'$PWD'\"],\"transcriptPath\":\"'$PWD'/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/'$CONV'/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl\",\"artifactDirectoryPath\":\"'$PWD'/.gemini/artifacts\",\"executionNum\":1,\"terminationReason\":\"model_stop\",\"error\":\"\",\"fullyIdle\":true}' | $ENTIRE hooks antigravity stop\n```\n\n**Expect:** Each hook prints log lines like `event=TurnStart session_id=smoke-... agent=antigravity`. Session state file appears at `.git/entire-sessions/<conv-id>.json`.\n\n## Phase 3: Walk every CLI command group\n\n```fish\n# status — does it show the session and the antigravity agent?\n$ENTIRE status\n\n# session group\n$ENTIRE session list\n$ENTIRE session info $CONV\n$ENTIRE session current\n\n# Commit the file — this triggers condensation\ngit add foo.txt\ngit commit -m \"antigravity smoke\"\n\n# checkpoint group — should now have one entry tagged antigravity\n$ENTIRE checkpoint list\n$ENTIRE checkpoint explain HEAD\n\n# agent group\n$ENTIRE agent list                    # ✓ antigravity\n$ENTIRE agent                         # bare opens picker\n\n# doctor — scan for issues\n$ENTIRE doctor\n\n# version\n$ENTIRE version\n\n# activity (recent agent activity)\n$ENTIRE activity\n```\n\n**Watch for:**\n- `entire status` should show antigravity as the active/configured agent\n- `entire checkpoint list` should show your commit with an `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer\n- `entire checkpoint explain HEAD` should show the prompt and transcript\n\n## Phase 4: Rewind round-trip\n\n```fish\n# Add another change\necho \"modified\" >> foo.txt\ngit add foo.txt && git commit -m \"second change\"\n\n# Rewind to first checkpoint\n$ENTIRE checkpoint list                # note the IDs\n$ENTIRE checkpoint rewind <first-id>   # interactive prompt\n\n# Verify foo.txt content reverted\ncat foo.txt\n```\n\n## Phase 5: Cleanup\n\n```fish\n# Remove hooks\n$ENTIRE agent remove antigravity\n\n# Verify .agents/hooks.json is empty (or has only foreign keys if you'd added any)\ncat .agents/hooks.json\n\n# Or nuke everything\n$ENTIRE clean\n```\n\n## What to report back\n\nTell me:\n- ✅ what works as expected\n- ❌ anything that misbehaves (with the exact command + output)\n- 🤔 anything that's confusing or feels off\n\nI'll leave the branch as-is in the meantime — no commits, no pushes, nothing destructive. When you're done smoke testing, we can come back to the finish-branch options (merge / push+PR / keep / discard).\n\nNote for the **agy real-binary test** — if `agy --print` is still timing out for you, you can try the interactive flow:\n```fish\n# In a separate terminal, with hooks installed:\ncd /tmp/agy-smoke\nagy\n# Then prompt agy to create a file, exit, and check `entire status` from another terminal\n```\n\nBut that's optional — the hook-driving smoke tests above exercise the full integration without needing agy to actually run."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":616213,"cache_read_input_tokens":21659,"output_tokens":3494,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":616213,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3494,"cache_read_input_tokens":21659,"cache_creation_input_tokens":616213,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":616213},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"system_changed","cache_missed_input_tokens":492613}}},"requestId":"req_011CbFwtfv