{"parentUuid":"36afc6a1-9bde-4f11-a6c2-c29ac3162990","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01D3X6k7HN5JgDfuzskrTpqS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- Yes, that's exactly the model: **hook configuration is workspace-scoped, not session-scoped**. Once `.agents/hooks.json` exists in the workspace, every `agy` session run from that directory automatically inherits the hooks. There's no per-session opt-in step.\n- The lifecycle is: `agy` starts → reads `.agents/hooks.json` → registers entries → fires them as events happen (PreInvocation → PreToolUse → PostToolUse → PostInvocation → Stop) → each invocation pipes a JSON payload to `entire hooks antigravity <event>` via stdin.\n- One catch worth knowing: the installed hook commands reference `entire` (not `/tmp/entire-smoke`). The wrapper `sh -c 'if ! command -v entire ...'` makes them gracefully no-op if `entire` isn't on PATH. That means **if `entire` isn't on PATH, your hooks will fire-and-noop silently** — you won't see errors, but you also won't see session state being captured.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nYes — `agy` is the right next step. But first verify the binary your hooks are calling is actually findable:\n\n```fish\n# Is 'entire' on PATH?\nwhich entire\n\n# If not (likely, since you're using /tmp/entire-smoke):\n# Option A: symlink the dev binary onto PATH\nln -sf /tmp/entire-smoke ~/.local/bin/entire   # or wherever your fish PATH includes\nwhich entire   # verify\n\n# Option B: install hooks in local-dev mode so they call `go run` against the source\n# (need to remove and re-add)\n$ENTIRE agent remove antigravity\n# There's probably a --local-dev or similar flag; check:\n$ENTIRE agent add --help\n```\n\nOnce `which entire` resolves, here's what to do next:\n\n```fish\n# Start agy interactively in this repo\ncd /tmp/agy-smoke\nagy\n```\n\nIn the agy session, give it a small task — something like:\n```\ncreate a file called hello.txt with the text \"world\", then exit\n```\n\n**What to watch for** (from another terminal — open a second tab to /tmp/agy-smoke):\n\n```fish\ncd /tmp/agy-smoke\n\n# 1. Did session state get created?\nls -la .git/entire-sessions/\n\n# 2. What's in it?\ncat .git/entire-sessions/*.json | jq .\n\n# 3. After agy exits and you commit, did a checkpoint land?\ngit add . && git commit -m \"agy session\"\n$ENTIRE checkpoint list\n\n# 4. Status shows the session\n$ENTIRE status\n```\n\n**Heads up about your earlier `agy --print` timeout:** that was the headless mode hanging on an async background search. Interactive mode (`agy` with no args) might behave better since you can see what it's doing and Ctrl-C without losing data. If it hangs on the same problem, give it a simpler prompt that doesn't trigger filesystem search — e.g., \"echo 'hi' > hi.txt and exit\".\n\nLet me know:\n- Whether `which entire` resolves (fix needed if no)\n- Whether agy starts and accepts input\n- Whether session state appears after the first turn"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1123,"cache_read_input_tokens":642545,"output_tokens":2229,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1123,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2229,"cache_read_input_tokens":642545,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1123,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1123},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CbG1YRyq8W46LWbft4hva","type":"assistant","uuid":"1263fe91-14b3-42f3-88bd-4a73367a0fb1","timestamp":"2026-05-21T16:14:22.529Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli","sessionId":